    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/student-scholarship-and-loans-officer-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Student Scholarship and Loans Officer",
      "description": "Student Scholarship and Loans Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Scholarship and Loans Officer 495958 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 25 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. We have an exciting opportunity for a motivated and detail-oriented Student Scholarships and Loans Officer to join the Student Services and Support Directorate. This role offers the opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to student success by administering scholarships, bursaries and other financial assistance programs that support equitable access to higher education. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba Campus HEWL 5: $78,740 - $89,310 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the Student Scholarships and Loans Officer, you will be responsible for the administration of scholarships, bursaries and financial assistance programs, ensuring accurate, timely and compliant outcomes for students and stakeholders. You will assess applications, provide advice and guidance, manage complex enquiries, and contribute to the promotion of scholarship opportunities across the University. Working closely with students, staff, donors and external stakeholders, you will play an important role in supporting student retention, participation and success. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring experience in a financial or administrative environment, together with strong organisational skills and a commitment to customer service excellence. You will have the ability to apply sound judgement when interpreting policies and procedures, manage competing priorities, and communicate effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. Experience administering scholarships, loans, bursaries or similar programs will be highly regarded, along with strong computer literacy and attention to detail. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us in the Student Services & Support Directorate. Click the ‘apply’ button and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Renee Simkins at renee.simkins@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 070ad006 Last Name (required) 5f76526e Email (required) 63c5d0dd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. WHS Support Officer (Fire & Emergency) Townsville Professional Join JCU’s Work Health and Safety team and support fire safety, emergency preparedness and first aid across the University. You’ll coordinate evacuation activities, undertake inspections and provide practical safety advice. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) b95dddbe Last Name (required) 6de05120 Email (required) 2ac353f6 Job Alert 68a72376 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Student Services & Support Student Services & Support Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do 