    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/whs-support-officer-fire-emergency-townsville-qld-australia-c35fe2cd-f365-4142-afac-5086f56b5c06": {
      "title": "WHS Support Officer (Fire & Emergency)",
      "description": "WHS Support Officer (Fire & Emergency) - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! WHS Support Officer (Fire & Emergency) 495913 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 19 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. This is a hands-on opportunity to help create a safe and resilient environment for JCU staff, students and visitors. You’ll support fire safety, emergency preparedness and first aid activities while providing practical advice to stakeholders across the University. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus HEWL 5: $78,740 - $89,310 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the WHS Support Officer (Fire and Emergency) , you will work within the Work Health and Safety team to support the University's fire safety, emergency management and first aid programs. You will help ensure these programs meet legislative requirements, Building Fire Safety Regulations and University safety standards. This varied role will see you coordinate evacuation drills, develop and maintain Emergency Evacuation Plans, support and train Emergency Control Organisation members, maintain emergency management plans and records, and undertake workplace inspections and audits. You will work with stakeholders across JCU to provide practical advice, support risk management activities and identify opportunities to strengthen emergency preparedness and safety practices. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring experience in fire safety, emergency management, workplace health and safety, or a related field, supported by a practical understanding of relevant legislation, standards and compliance requirements. You will be a qualified Fire Safety Advisor or have an equivalent combination of relevant experience and training. Your experience will include coordinating evacuation drills, conducting workplace inspections and audits, and maintaining first aid kits, defibrillators and other emergency response equipment. You will be able to identify risks, investigate incidents and recommend practical improvements that support positive safety outcomes. You will also be a clear and confident communicator who can build effective working relationships with people from a range of backgrounds. You will be comfortable delivering training and inductions, managing changing priorities, and working both independently and as part of a team. Additional qualifications in work health and safety, training and assessment, first aid or fire safety will be highly regarded. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Andrew Reddicliffe at andrew.reddicliffe@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) ca20b08b Last Name (required) c830a70f Email (required) 43c88173 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 696a2b22 Last Name (required) f6cb4540 Email (required) 3746926e Job Alert 408cee7f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Work Health & Safety Work Health & Safety Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
