    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/research-training-and-researcher-development-advisor-townsville-qld-australia-3114b029-fa56-444f-9f14-a0891b9d3676": {
      "title": "Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor",
      "description": "Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor 495426 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 18 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description 12-month fixed-term contract Full-time – 36.25 hours per week HEWL 8 – $111,960 – $128,567 + 17% superannuation and great benefits Based in Townsville – applicants must be currently based in Townsville Current JCU students are not eligible to apply At James Cook University (JCU) , we are committed to creating a brighter future for the people of Northern Australia and the Tropics worldwide. As Australia’s leading tropical university, our research tackles some of the world’s most pressing challenges and creates meaningful impact for communities locally and globally. We are seeking an enthusiastic and innovative Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor to join the Graduate Research School within the Research Division. In this rewarding role, you'll play a pivotal part in enhancing the experience of Higher Degree by Research (HDR) candidates, researchers and research support staff through engaging research training and researcher development initiatives. Why you'll love this role This is an opportunity to make a real difference to JCU's research community. You'll design and deliver impactful learning experiences, foster meaningful connections across the University, and help develop the skills and capabilities of emerging and established researchers. You'll join a highly collaborative environment where creativity, innovation and continuous improvement are valued, working alongside passionate colleagues dedicated to research excellence. What you'll be doing As the Research Training and Researcher Development Advisor , you will: Design and deliver contemporary research training and researcher development programs across multiple campuses and online platforms. Create engaging learning materials and content that maximise participant engagement and learning outcomes. Build strong partnerships across the University and with external stakeholders to source expert presenters and facilitators. Evaluate program effectiveness, analyse feedback and outcomes, and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Collaborate across the University to strengthen pathways into Higher Degree by Research programs and support successful research outcomes. Contribute to the strategic objectives and success of the Graduate Research School, Research Division and the broader University. What you'll bring We're looking for someone who is passionate about learning, community building and supporting researcher success. You will demonstrate: Experience working within a university or research-focused environment and an understanding of the needs of researchers and research students. Outstanding communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage diverse stakeholders. Experience developing networks, fostering community engagement and coordinating events, workshops or professional development activities. Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities, with a focus on continuous improvement and innovation. Excellent written and digital communication skills, including developing engaging online content and learning resources. Why James Cook University? At JCU, our people are at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to developing the skills, knowledge and capability of our staff while fostering a culture of respect, excellence and sustainability. When you join JCU, you'll become part of a university that is: Driven by purpose and impact. Committed to research excellence and innovation. Focused on creating opportunities for growth and professional development. Guided by the values of Excellence, Authenticity, Integrity and Respect . You'll enjoy: A collaborative and supportive team environment. Flexible work arrangements where operationally appropriate. Generous superannuation and leave entitlements. Professional development opportunities. Ready to make a difference? If you're excited about empowering researchers, building vibrant learning communities and contributing to world-class research outcomes, we'd love to hear from you. please note that this position is based in Townsville and applicants must be currently based in Townsville. Current JCU students are not eligible to apply for this position. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the online application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your experience and how your skills align with the role. For more information, please contact Gabby Ryan via email at gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au . Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/business-improvement-officer-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Business Improvement Officer",
      "description": "Business Improvement Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Business Improvement Officer 495484 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 13 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Make a visible difference across JCU by leading improvement initiatives from problem identification through to implementation and benefits realisation. Working primarily from our Townsville campus, you will collaborate with operational teams and leaders to simplify processes, improve services and embed better ways of working, including opportunities supported by automation, AI and digital tools. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based on-site at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As Business Improvement Officer , you will help drive meaningful improvements across JCU by partnering with teams to identify opportunities, solve operational challenges and improve the way work gets done. Working across a diverse range of services, you will lead improvement initiatives from opportunity identification through to implementation, benefits realisation and transition into business-as-usual operations. Success in this role comes from working alongside operational teams to understand how services are delivered, identify practical opportunities for improvement and support the implementation of sustainable solutions that deliver measurable outcomes. This is a hands-on improvement role focused on achieving results, not simply analysing problems. You will help build capability, support change and embed new ways of working that improve service delivery, efficiency and customer experience. Based on-site at JCU's Bebegu Yumba campus in Townsville, this is a visible, relationship-focused role that suits someone who enjoys being in the business, building connections and working directly with people to make a tangible difference. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE A passion for improving services, solving problems and helping people achieve better outcomes. This role will suit an experienced continuous improvement practitioner who enjoys working directly with operational teams and turning improvement opportunities into practical, sustainable results. Experience leading improvement initiatives from opportunity identification through to implementation and benefits realisation will be highly regarded. Success in the role requires a practical, delivery-focused approach and the ability to engage stakeholders, build momentum and maintain focus on outcomes. Strong relationship-building, facilitation and problem-solving skills will enable you to collaborate effectively with leaders, subject matter experts and frontline teams. Experience applying approaches such as Lean, process mapping, root cause analysis and benefits measurement will support your ability to translate complexity into achievable actions and measurable improvements. Motivation comes from seeing change successfully implemented, adopted and sustained. A collaborative approach, resilience and an ability to influence through credibility and trust will be key to helping teams embrace new ways of working and deliver lasting benefits. An interest in AI, automation, workflow technologies and other digital solutions will be valuable. While technical expertise is not essential, the ability to recognise opportunities and partner with specialists to deliver practical business outcomes will support success in the role. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and suitable candidates may be progressed before the closing date. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Lauren Tapp at lauren.tapp@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) dd4804cc Last Name (required) aff4375e Email (required) 995137b4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 82352096 Last Name (required) acb68f5d Email (required) 31cfc5a6 Job Alert bc713d6b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Service Transformation & Client Satisfaction Service Transformation & Client Satisfaction Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
