    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/associate-lecturer-lecturer-physiotherapy-townsville-qld-australia-f9eef323-03eb-46b0-87a0-f94b63124666": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer / Lecturer, Physiotherapy",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer / Lecturer, Physiotherapy - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate Lecturer / Lecturer, Physiotherapy 495818 Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Academic Level A or B | Full-time (36.25 hours per week)| Townsville Lead teaching in acute care and cardiorespiratory physiotherapy. Prepare future physiotherapists for practice in rural and remote communities. Join a collaborative healthcare education team at Australia’s University for the Tropics. Academic Level A $80,371 - $107,395 Academic Level B $112,810 - $133,110 + 17% Super, 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading and other great benefits Bring your clinical expertise and passion for education to a role where you can influence the next generation of physiotherapists. You will deliver essential teaching in acute care, cardiorespiratory and rural and remote physiotherapy, helping ensure JCU graduates develop the knowledge and practical capabilities required for professional practice. About the role As Associate Lecturer/Lecturer, Physiotherapy , you will coordinate and deliver undergraduate and/or postgraduate teaching, with a particular focus on acute care, cardiorespiratory and rural and remote physiotherapy practice. Your contribution will support the delivery of these important areas of practice to the standard required for program accreditation. You will develop and review contemporary learning materials, deliver practical classes and tutorials, coordinate subjects, assess student learning and provide academic and pastoral support. Depending on your level of appointment, you will also have opportunities to develop your scholarship and research profile, supervise Honours and postgraduate students, contribute to grant applications and collaborate with clinicians, researchers and community partners. Key responsibilities Prepare and deliver engaging undergraduate and/or postgraduate teaching in acute care, cardiorespiratory and rural and remote physiotherapy. Coordinate subjects and undertake assessment and moderation in accordance with University policies and accreditation requirements. Develop and review learning materials to support contemporary, evidence-informed physiotherapy education. Deliver face-to-face practical classes, tutorials and online learning activities. Provide academic guidance and pastoral support that enables students to succeed. Develop scholarship and research activities within your areas of expertise. Build collaborative relationships with clinicians, researchers and professional networks. Supervise Honours and postgraduate students, as appropriate to the level of appointment. Contribute to the academic, administrative and collegial activities of the Discipline of Physiotherapy and the College of Healthcare Sciences. About you You are an enthusiastic physiotherapy professional who is passionate about developing capable, work-ready graduates. You enjoy sharing your clinical knowledge, creating practical learning experiences and working collaboratively within an interprofessional environment. To be successful in this role, you will have: A qualification in Physiotherapy and eligibility for registration with AHPRA Clinical experience in physiotherapy practice, ideally including acute care, cardiorespiratory and/or rural and remote settings. Strong communication, organisation and problem-solving skills. The ability to work effectively both independently and within an interprofessional team. A commitment to high-quality physiotherapy education and student success. Additional Requirements for Academic Level B In addition to the above, Level B applicants will have: A postgraduate qualification in Physiotherapy or a related field, or equivalent experience in physiotherapy education. Experience in curriculum development, teaching innovation and quality assurance. Experience coordinating subjects and contributing to academic administration and governance. The capacity to supervise Honours and/or postgraduate research students. Why work at JCU As Australia’s University for the Tropics, JCU offers a purpose-driven and collaborative environment where your clinical experience and teaching can make a meaningful difference. The College of Healthcare Sciences supports quality teaching and research across physiotherapy and other allied health disciplines. This role provides an opportunity to contribute directly to workforce capability by preparing physiotherapists for the diverse needs of acute, rural and remote healthcare settings. JCU offers: Five weeks annual leave plus leave loading Flexible work arrangements Up to 12 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Paid study leave and staff development programs Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program, including coaching and counselling How to Apply Click the Apply button and: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant clinical and teaching experience, including your experience in acute care, cardiorespiratory and/or rural and remote physiotherapy practice, and how your skills will support your success in the role. For enquiries about the role, please contact Dr Anne Jones on (07) 4781 4085 or via email anne.jones@jcu.edu.au JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive and welcoming environment. We encourage applications from candidates who meet the requirements of the role and share our commitment to excellence in physiotherapy education. Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/casual-eoi-laboratory-and-technical-support-townsville-qld-australia-cairns": {
      "title": "Casual EOI",
      "description": "Casual EOI - Laboratory and Technical Support - Townsville, QLD, Australia - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Casual EOI - Laboratory and Technical Support 495002 Cairns Townsville Professional Casual Closing on: Oct 31 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Expression of Interest – Casual Laboratory and Technical Support Creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally, James Cook University (JCU) is seeking Expressions of Interest for Laboratory and Technical Support to support practical learning and  teaching activities across a variety of discipline areas including medicine, nursing and allied health, engineering, animal handling, aquaculture and across the sciences. What You Can Accomplish in the Role In this role, you will deliver high-quality technical support that enables undergraduate and postgraduate teaching to achieve academic objectives, helping to provide students with a hands-on, practical learning experience. You will contribute to: Supporting undergraduate classes, field trips, intensives, and workshops, ensuring activities are delivered on time and in accordance with established procedures. Maintaining safe and compliant teaching and research environments through cleaning, waste management, equipment servicing, and sterilisation. Ensuring Workplace Health and Safety (WHS) requirements are understood and adhered to within laboratory settings. Providing guidance to staff and students on laboratory procedures, policies, and relevant legislative requirements. Supporting continuous improvement by contributing to service enhancements and evaluating user outcomes and satisfaction. What You Can Bring to the Role You are a proactive and reliable professional with strong technical and organisational skills, and a commitment to delivering high-quality support services. You will bring: Relevant qualifications and/or experience related to the discipline Experience in standard laboratory and/or field techniques, including familiarity with common laboratory and field equipment. Sound understanding of WHS legislation and its practical application within laboratory environments. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Effective communication and interpersonal skills, with a commitment to delivering a customer-focused service. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a high-volume environment. Strong computer skills, including Microsoft Office, and the ability to learn new systems quickly with attention to detail. Additional Requirements Current First Aid Certificate Current Queensland C Class Driver Licence Current Working with Children Blue Card Specific certifications and vaccinations may be required for some roles* Why Submit an Expression of Interest? This Expression of Interest will be used to establish a talent pool for upcoming opportunities within JCU. If you’re passionate about supporting teaching and research through technical expertise, we encourage you to apply. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 46d2b6d9 Last Name (required) be053632 Email (required) c2eb6d3c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 12a8a8b2 Last Name (required) 026f395c Email (required) 329be00f Job Alert 668c21d1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Services Academic Services Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Cairns, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Cairns, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
